ents-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:c1828ce90c9b43ee66ac5fad3d6d72087a8b3bf3adfa60143f45668141da9367","file":"preprints/Optimal-order-mixing-of-the-Thorp-shuffle-September-26-2026/build/main.tex","line":486,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"fb6ec1448e59181c4802a91bd2258ccdb3d4af8b2788974a72b6ca97a1181c47","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Optimal-order-mixing-of-the-Thorp-shuffle-September-26-2026/build/main.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:c1828ce90c9b43ee66ac5fad3d6d72087a8b3bf3adfa60143f45668141da9367","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Optimal-order-mixing-of-the-Thorp-shuffle-September-26-2026/build/main.tex#L486"},"statement_kind":"proposition","text":"\\label{prop:orbit-lift}\nLet \\(n\\) be a positive multiple of eight, and partition the labels of \\(G=S_n\\) into sets \\(M_1,\\ldots,M_8\\) of size \\(n/8\\). For each \\(a\\), let \\(H_a\\) be the subgroup fixing every label outside \\(M_a\\). Suppose a probability measure \\(\\nu\\) on \\(G\\) satisfies\n\\[\n \\nu(gH_a)\\le4\\frac{|H_a|}{|G|}\n \\qquad(g\\in G,\\ 1\\le a\\le8).\n\\]\nThen every irreducible unitary representation \\(\\rho\\) of \\(G\\), of degree \\(D\\), satisfies\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:h-12}\n \\|\\widehat\\nu(\\rho)\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}\n \\le A D^{-5/16},\\qquad A=\\sqrt{32C_1}.\n\\end{equation}"}
